27 0 obj
<< /A 567 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing recruitment and randomization of 283 individuals, with 66 randomized into two equal groups for experimental and sham EA intervention; primary reasons for exclusion, dropouts, and intention-to-treat analysis sets are detailed.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 20 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 568 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing least-square mean change from baseline over twenty-eight weeks for EA Group and Sham EA Group. EA Group shows a consistent decrease, while Sham EA Group remains stable then increases. Error bars indicate confidence intervals. Sample sizes \(n\) decrease over time for both groups.) /K 1 /P 9 0 R /Pg 23 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 569 0 R /Alt (Four grouped bar graphs labeled A, B, C, and D compare least-square mean changes from baseline in various measures between the EA group \(dark blue\) and Sham EA group \(light blue\). Panels A and B display changes in ADLs Total, Subscale BADLs, and Subscale IADLs, while panels C and D show NPI Frequency × Severity, NPI Frequency, NPI Severity, and NPI Caregiver Distress; error bars reflect 95 percent confidence intervals. A legend identifies EA and Sham EA groups.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 23 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
